<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Home Church, the app's entitlements.

  WHAT THIS IS AND WHY IT IS IN THE REPO. One key, `aps-environment`, which is
  what actually grants an app the right to register for push notifications.
  Without it iOS does not refuse the registration and does not raise an error.
  It simply never calls back. Permission says granted, `register()` resolves,
  and no token ever arrives, which is the single most misleading failure in
  this whole feature: everything looks like it worked.

  This file was missing for the entire life of the project and cost an evening
  to find. Adding the Push Notifications capability in Xcode is supposed to
  create it, and the capability can end up listed in Signing & Capabilities
  while the file itself was never written or never linked. Nothing else in the
  app can tell, so nothing else could report it.

  WHY IT LIVES HERE rather than in ios/. Same reason as PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
  next to it: ios/ is generated and gitignored, so a hand written file inside
  it is destroyed the first time somebody runs `npx cap add ios` again. Kept
  here, it survives, and scripts/preflight.js checks it is still here.

  WHERE IT GOES. Once ios/ exists:

      cp ios-config/App.entitlements ios/App/App/

  Then in Xcode, App target -> Build Settings -> search "entitlements" ->
  set Code Signing Entitlements to `App/App.entitlements`. XCODE.md step 8
  spells this out with where to click.

  WHY THE VALUE SAYS development AND THAT IS CORRECT FOR THE APP STORE TOO.
  A build Xcode puts on a device plugged into your Mac is a development build
  and registers against Apple's sandbox push gateway. When you archive for
  distribution, the signing process rewrites this entitlement to `production`
  from the distribution provisioning profile. So this file says development
  and a shipped build still gets production, and you do not edit it before
  submitting. The thing you DO have to change for the two gateways is the
  APNS_HOST secret on the send-push Edge Function, which is a separate switch
  and is written up in LAUNCH_TODO.md under "Push notifications".
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
